📊 Power BI Project: Retail Order & Delivery Performance Dashboard
 Project Title
Retail Sales & Delivery Performance Analysis Dashboard
________________________________________
1️⃣ Project Objective
To analyze:
•	Sales performance
•	Product performance
•	Order status trends
•	Delivery efficiency
•	Payment method usage
•	Discount impact on revenue
And help management:
•	Improve delivery time
•	Identify top-selling products
•	Reduce cancellations
•	Increase revenue
________________________________________
2️⃣Dataset Description
Column	Description
OrderID	Unique order number
CustomerID	Unique customer ID
ProductID	Unique product ID
ProductName	Name of product
StoreID	Store identifier
DeliveryPartnerID	Delivery partner ID
OrderDate	Date of order
DeliveryDate	Delivery completion date
UnitPrice	Price per item
Quantity	Units ordered
TotalPrice	UnitPrice × Quantity
DiscountApplied	Discount amount
DeliveryTimeMinutes	Time taken to deliver
OrderStatus	Delivered / Pending / Cancelled
PaymentMethodID	Payment method used
TimeOfDay	Morning / Afternoon / Evening
________________________________________
3️⃣ Data Cleaning in Power BI (Power Query)
✔ Convert Data Types
•	OrderDate → Date
•	DeliveryDate → Date
•	UnitPrice → Decimal
•	Quantity → Whole Number
•	TotalPrice → Decimal
•	DiscountApplied → Decimal
•	DeliveryTimeMinutes → Whole Number
✔ Create New Columns
🔹 1. Net Revenue
Net Revenue = TotalPrice - DiscountApplied
🔹 2. Delivery Delay (if needed)
Delivery Days = DATEDIFF(OrderDate, DeliveryDate, DAY)
________________________________________
4️⃣ DAX Measures (Important for Interview)
📌 Total Revenue
Total Revenue = SUM(order_transactions[TotalPrice])
📌 Total Discount
Total Discount = SUM(order_transactions[DiscountApplied])
📌 Net Revenue
Net Revenue = [Total Revenue] - [Total Discount]
📌 Total Orders
Total Orders = COUNT(order_transactions[OrderID])
📌 Delivered Orders
Delivered Orders = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNT(order_transactions[OrderID]),
    order_transactions[OrderStatus] = "Delivered"
)
📌 Cancellation Rate
Cancellation Rate = 
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(COUNT(order_transactions[OrderID]),
    order_transactions[OrderStatus] = "Cancelled"),
    [Total Orders]
)
📌 Average Delivery Time
Avg Delivery Time = 
AVERAGE(order_transactions[DeliveryTimeMinutes])
